  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\n\nSubtle height rises return for Tuesday as the mid-level wave departs \nthe area. Sfc high pressure builds in too which should lead to dry \nconditions for most locations. A more compact H5 shortwave is seen \nriding the southwesterly flow for the second half of Tuesday across \nour far southeast: NBM guidance keys in on some precip chances (15-\n30%) for our far south and eastern areas where the wave traverses.\n\nMore mid-level disturbances ride the southwesterly to slightly zonal \nflow Wednesday through Friday which will lead to periodic chances \nfor rain showers (30-50%). H8 warm advection and moisture transport \nlingers in the general vicinity during that timeframe too. Late \nFriday into Saturday, models indicate another compact wave \ntraversing the area. NBM during this period suggests a good 50 to \n60% chance for rain areawide. \n\nHighs largely range from the 60s and 70s for most of the long term \nperiod. Wednesday through Friday appear to be the warmest with most \nareas hitting the low to mid 70s. Late next weekend, highs cool to \nthe 60s.",
